{
 "note": "R82a - ABKC sample-record grammar re-read on every loose PS3 `.abk` (NHL 11 / 14 / 15 / Legacy), to explain the R80 chant entry-1\nresidual and to state the record classes the 2026-09-20 handoff 02 did not. Read-only; every entry of every table (not a sample).\n\nGrammar under test (derived from the PS3 NHL 15 bytes, then tested here on all four trees):\n  table:  'S10A' | u32 0 | u32 count | u32 header length = 16 + 4*(count-1) (0 when count = 0) | (count-1) x u32 offset of samples\n          2..n relative to the table start; offset 0xFFFFFFFF = absent slot (no record). Records are NOT padded; the table's data size\n          (file word 0x24) is 4-aligned, so the last record may end 0-3 bytes before table start + data size.\n  record: SNR h1 | SNR h2 (type = h2 >> 30, loop = bit 29, num_samples = low 29 bits), then by type:\n    ram (0):     [u32 loop_start when loop] | segments{ u32 size (counts the 8 SNR bytes) | u32 samples | (size - 8) codec bytes }\n                 repeated until sum(samples) == num_samples (one segment for non-loop records; loop records carry one or two -\n                 an intro segment of loop_start samples then the loop body);\n    stream (1):  8 bytes, or 16 with the loop bit (u32 a | u32 b); no size, no inline audio - the audio is in the sibling `<bank>.ast`.\n  codec 0x05 segment = one EALayer3 v1 block per R77: channel_config 0 -> mono; 1 -> stereo (2-channel side info); 3 -> two stereo\n  EA-frame streams interleaved frame by frame (two warm-up frames, two 47-sample PCM frames, granules x 576 = 2 x (samples + 1152 + trim)).\nTests, per entry:\n  T1 record ends exactly at the next present entry's offset (last entry: 0-3 bytes before the data end);\n  T2 (ram) every segment's `samples` word sums to num_samples; single-segment non-loop records have samples == num_samples;\n  T3 (ram, codec 0x05) every segment tiles under R77 and its granule count matches the channel class\n      (cc 0 / 1: G + 47 - samples = 1152 + trim, 0 <= trim < 4 * 576; cc 3: G + 94 - 2 * samples = 2304 + trim, 0 <= trim < 8 * 576;\n      the trim distribution is recorded per class);\n  T4 (ram loop) loop_start == 0 for one segment, == segment-1 samples for two segments;\n  T5 (stream entries) the sibling `.ast`: header 'S10S' + u32, data from 0x40 as a chain of blocks (u8 flags | u24 size | u32 word),\n      walked to the file end or not; blocks with flag 0x80 counted against the bank's stream entries. Observation only - no join claimed.\nUsage: python r82_abk_entry_records.py <out.json>\n",
